
# GIT BEST PRACTICES

## Good Commit Messages

- Commit messages should describe what changed.

- Good:

    Add user registration

    Fix incorrect password validation

    Add database indexes

    Update README installation instructions

- Avoid vague messages such as:

    stuff

    update

    changes

    fixed things

---

## Commit Frequently

- I should make commits regularly.

- A commit should represent a logical change.

- Example:

    Commit 1:
    Add database model

    Commit 2:
    Add registration form

    Commit 3:
    Add password validation

- This makes it easier to understand and undo changes.

---

## Keep Commits Focused

- A commit should ideally do one main thing.

- Bad:

    Add login + redesign homepage + fix database + update README

- Better:

    Add login system

    Fix database connection

    Redesign homepage

    Update README

- Focused commits make code reviews and debugging easier.

